  "id": "regret-theory",
  "term": "regret theory",
  "definition": "Regret theory is a decision-making approach that considers not only the expected benefit of a choice but also the regret a person may expect to feel if another option would have been better. It is used to account for how anticipated regret can shape choices, including comparisons with similar past cases.",
